# Supabase and database

- Inspect existing migrations and generated types before changing schema.
- Add new migrations; do not rewrite migrations that may be deployed.
- Use snake_case for database fields.
- Preserve legacy data through backfills before enforcing new constraints.
- Add constraints only after existing data is compatible.
- Ensure RLS policies cover SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, and DELETE as appropriate.
- Test cross-workspace access denial.
- Use transactions or equivalent atomic operations for credits and paid generation.
- Maintain created_at and updated_at conventions already used by the repository.
- Document destructive or irreversible changes.
